.lake/
workspace/
formalization-graph.json
conformance.json
ledger-*.json
sacm-*.json
mutation.json
audit.json
fvspec-report.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# never commit credentials
.env
*.key
Autoform/Generated/Scale*.lean
contracts-*.json

# The mutation gate writes this beside the module it is rewriting, as the pristine copy
# to restore from if a run is interrupted. It is scratch state for a run in flight and
# must never be committed -- a commit taken mid-run would capture a mutant's backup as
# though it were the module.
*.mutate-backup

# The neutral AST is NOT ignored, and after the 2026-08-19 policy change below it is the
# *only* tracked half of the AST/module pair -- so ignoring it would leave nothing at all
# to check a build against from a clean clone. Keep ast-*.json tracked.

# --- Generated Lean modules: build products, not tracked (decided 2026-08-19) ---
#
# Autoform/Generated/<M>.lean is a deterministic function of ast-<M>.json --
# render_lean.py is verified byte-identical across runs -- so tracking it stores no
# information the AST does not already determine. What it DID buy was a write channel:
# the mutation-gate mutant that survived four commits reached git precisely because the
# module was tracked, and a 21 MB machine-generated file has no reviewable diff. Ansible
# (21 MB) and LinuxLib (6 MB) were swept in by a `git add -A` during a merge today.
#
# Policy: the AST is the tracked source of truth. artifact-manifest.json pins the sha256
# of each AST and of its render; scripts/check_render.py verifies both and can
# materialise + type-check the render. See docs/integrity.md.
Autoform/Generated/*.lean
# Exception: Cachetools is the one module hand-written theorems depend on by name, and at
# 300 KB its diff is still reviewable -- the two conditions under which tracking a render
# earns its drift risk. It stays tracked and check_render.py diffs it every run.
!Autoform/Generated/Cachetools.lean
# Exception: SC.lean has no ast-SC.json anywhere in the repo, so the AST-only policy has
# nothing to regenerate it from. Untracking it would delete it outright rather than move
# it upstream. It stays tracked until it has a source, and check_render.py cannot speak
# for it (no AST, no verdict) -- which is itself the reason it should acquire one.
!Autoform/Generated/SC.lean

# ASTs for the large corpora. ast-*.json is otherwise TRACKED and must stay so -- it is
# now the only tracked half of the pair. These four are 15-55 MB each, i.e. larger than
# the modules they render to, so they are tracked by sha256 + provenance in
# artifact-manifest.json instead of by bytes, and check_render.py reports them
# UNVERIFIABLE (loudly, non-zero) rather than passing when the AST is not on disk.
ast-Ansible.json
ast-LinuxLib.json
ast-LinuxCrypto.json
# ast-V8Base.json is TRACKED: 3.2 MB, and 74 spec files / 285 theorems under
# Autoform/SpecsGen/V8Base/ are tracked and pinned to it. Tracked theorems whose
# corpus no clone can produce are unverifiable (STRATEGY 55).
!ast-V8Base.json

# Hypothesis's example database, written by scripts/synth_specs.py when it borrows
# Hypothesis as a value generator. Run state, not source.
.hypothesis/

# Tracked exceptions to "track the AST, not the render": these two are tiny (4 and 7
# functions), proofs in Autoform/Specs and Autoform/SpecsGen name them directly, and
# tracking them is what lets the repository build from a clean clone -- the root import
# graph reaches them. The full V8Base/LinuxLib renders remain build products.
!Autoform/Generated/V8BaseSample.lean
!Autoform/Generated/LinuxLibSample.lean
!Autoform/Generated/CMath.lean

# Agent worktrees: full checkouts of this repository (12 GB). Never tracked;
# also excluded from audit_all.py's source sweep, see STRATEGY.md 56.
.claude/
